{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"web_search_instructions":"Find current Scalable Press API v2 design endpoint documentation, especially accepted artwork file formats, authentication, and quote/order request fields for DTG products."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"web_search_instructions":"Find current Scalable Press API v2 design endpoint documentation, especially accepted artwork file formats, authentication, and quote/order request fields for DTG products."},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: Scalable Press API v2 Design Endpoint Documentation\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nScalable Press offers a comprehensive API v2 that facilitates the creation and management of print designs, particularly for Direct-to-Garment (DTG) products. The Design API endpoint allows users to submit design specifications, including artwork files, and receive a unique design ID for order processing. Key aspects include accepted artwork file formats, authentication methods, and required fields for quote and order requests.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **Finding 1:** The Design API accepts artwork files in formats such as PNG and JPG, with a minimum resolution of 300 DPI to ensure print quality. ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/blog/solving-common-print-on-demand-integration-issues/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 2:** Authentication for the API is conducted via HTTP Basic Authentication, requiring the API key as the password and leaving the username blank. ([apis.apievangelist.com](https://apis.apievangelist.com/store/scalablepress-order-api/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 3:** When creating a design object for DTG products, essential fields include the design type ('dtg'), artwork file, dimensions (width or height), and position details. ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 4:** The API supports various product types, including screenprint, DTG, case, mug, and poster, each with specific design requirements. ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Source Analysis\n\n### Source 1: API Documentation\n\n- **URL:** ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Domain:** scalablepress.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Official Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official API documentation from Scalable Press)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Scalable Press API documentation provides detailed instructions on creating design objects for various product types, including DTG. It outlines the required fields such as design type, artwork file, dimensions, and position. The documentation also specifies that designs cannot be modified once created and emphasizes the necessity of authentication headers in API requests.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Design types supported: screenprint, dtg, case, mug, poster\n\n- Required fields for design object: type, sides (including artwork, dimensions, position)\n\n- Authentication method: HTTP Basic Authentication\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Designs cannot be modified once created.\"\n\n> \"Authentication headers are required.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 2: Solving Common Print-on-Demand Integration Issues\n\n- **URL:** ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/blog/solving-common-print-on-demand-integration-issues/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Domain:** scalablepress.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Approximately 1.4 years ago\n\n- **Source Type:** Blog Post\n\n- **Credibility:** Medium (Official blog post, but not primary documentation)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThis blog post addresses common integration issues with print-on-demand services, emphasizing the importance of consistent and accurate data formatting. It highlights the necessity of adhering to specific product data formats and image requirements to prevent errors and delays in order processing.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Accepted artwork file formats: PNG, JPG\n\n- Minimum resolution: 300 DPI\n\n- Importance of standardized product attributes for order handling\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Properly formatted images are key to maintaining print quality and avoiding processing errors.\"\n\n> \"Ensure product attributes follow a standardized format to streamline order handling.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 3: Scalable Press Order API\n\n- **URL:** ([apis.apievangelist.com](https://apis.apievangelist.com/store/scalablepress-order-api/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Domain:** apis.apievangelist.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** API Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** Medium (Third-party documentation)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Scalable Press Order API documentation provides information on placing and managing print-and-ship orders. It details the authentication method, which involves HTTP Basic Authentication using the API key as the password. The documentation also outlines various operations such as creating, retrieving, and canceling orders.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Authentication method: HTTP Basic Authentication\n\n- Operations supported: create, retrieve, cancel orders\n\n- Base URL: https://api.scalablepress.com/v2\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Supply your private Scalable Press API key as the password; the username is left blank.\"\n\n> \"Requests are made against a single base URL, `https://api.scalablepress.com`.\"\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Reference Analysis\n\n**Consensus Across Sources:**\n\n- All sources agree on the necessity of HTTP Basic Authentication using the API key as the password. ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- The requirement for artwork files to be in PNG or JPG format with a minimum resolution of 300 DPI is consistently emphasized. ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/blog/solving-common-print-on-demand-integration-issues/?utm_source=openai))\n\n**Conflicting Information:**\n\n- No significant conflicting information was identified among the sources.\n\n**Information Gaps:**\n\n- Specific details regarding the maximum file size for artwork uploads are not provided.\n\n- Clarification on whether additional authentication methods are supported beyond HTTP Basic Authentication is lacking.\n\n---\n\n## Research Metadata\n\n- **Search Completed:** 2026-08-23T03:22:52Z\n\n- **Sources Analyzed:** 3 sources\n\n- **Total Content Reviewed:** Approximately 1,200 words\n\n- **Search Confidence:** High (Based on the credibility and consistency of the sources)\n\n--- "}],"_meta":{"openai/widgetSessionId":"7abdf16c-9188-4771-a5aa-2f826f9a0e0c"},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
