{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"web_search_instructions":"Find Scalable Press API v2 quote request example for DTG: exact address field names and product size/color values. Focus on official docs or examples."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"web_search_instructions":"Find Scalable Press API v2 quote request example for DTG: exact address field names and product size/color values. Focus on official docs or examples."},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: Scalable Press API v2 DTG Quote Request Example\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nScalable Press provides a comprehensive API for obtaining Direct-to-Garment (DTG) printing quotes. The API requires specific fields for product details, shipping address, and design information to generate accurate quotes. Official documentation offers detailed examples and guidelines for these requests.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **Finding 1:** The Quote API requires product details including `id`, `color`, `quantity`, and `size` to generate a DTG quote.\n\n- **Finding 2:** Shipping address fields must include `name`, `address1`, `city`, `state`, and `zip` to process the quote request.\n\n- **Finding 3:** A valid `designId` is essential for an order-ready quote; omitting it results in a quote-only scenario.\n\n- **Finding 4:** The API supports multiple printing methods, including DTG, screen printing, and sublimation, allowing flexibility in product customization.\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Source Analysis\n\n### Source 1: API Documentation\n\n- **URL:** [https://scalablepress.com/docs/](https://scalablepress.com/docs/)\n\n- **Domain:** scalablepress.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Official Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official source from Scalable Press)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Scalable Press API documentation outlines the process for obtaining quotes for DTG printing. It specifies the required fields for product details, shipping address, and design information. The documentation provides example requests and responses, illustrating both order-ready and quote-only scenarios. It also details the API's capabilities, including support for multiple printing methods and custom order features.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Product details required: `id`, `color`, `quantity`, `size`\n\n- Shipping address fields: `name`, `address1`, `city`, `state`, `zip`\n\n- Design information: `designId`\n\n- Example response includes fields like `total`, `subtotal`, `tax`, `fees`, `shipping`, and `orderToken`\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Standard quotes allow a single design printed on one or more products, shipped to a single address.\"\n\n> \"A valid `designId` is essential for an order-ready quote; omitting it results in a quote-only scenario.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 2: Developer API | Print & Ship Products with Simple API Calls\n\n- **URL:** [https://scalablepress.com/api](https://scalablepress.com/api)\n\n- **Domain:** scalablepress.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Official Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official source from Scalable Press)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThis source provides an overview of the Scalable Press API, emphasizing its capabilities in programmatically sending customized products. It highlights the API's support for various printing methods, including DTG, and outlines the process for creating design objects, obtaining quotes, and placing orders. The documentation includes example requests and responses, demonstrating the API's functionality.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- API supports multiple printing methods: DTG, screen printing, sublimation\n\n- Process includes creating a design object, obtaining a quote, and placing an order\n\n- Example request for creating a design object includes fields like `type`, `sides[front][artwork]`, `sides[front][dimensions][width]`, `sides[front][position][horizontal]`, and `sides[front][position][offset][top]`\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Upload an artwork file, along with dimensions and placement specifications, to create a design object.\"\n\n> \"This design object can then be used to get quotes, create mockups, and place orders.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 3: Scalable Press Integration - Order Desk Knowledge Base\n\n- **URL:** [https://help.orderdesk.com/integration-setup-guides/print-on-demand/scalable-press-integration/](https://help.orderdesk.com/integration-setup-guides/print-on-demand/scalable-press-integration/)\n\n- **Domain:** help.orderdesk.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Approximately 1.1 years ago\n\n- **Source Type:** Knowledge Base\n\n- **Credibility:** Medium (Third-party integration guide)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThis knowledge base article provides guidance on integrating Scalable Press with Order Desk. It details the necessary fields for preparing orders and items, including product SKU, design ID, print type, color, and size. The article also covers dynamic printing options and the required fields for artwork files, print locations, and dimensions.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Required item fields: `print_sku`, `print_design_id`, `print_type`, `color`, `size`\n\n- Dynamic printing fields: `print_url`, `print_location`, `print_resize`, `print_preview`, `print_width`, `print_height`, `print_position`, `print_bottom_offset`, `print_top_offset`, `print_colors`\n\n- Artwork files should be 150 DPI PNG; screenprint should be EPS files\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"The following fields can be set as variations or item metadata for each item in an order.\"\n\n> \"If you don’t have a `print_design_id` field, you can use Order Desk to create one.\"\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Reference Analysis\n\n**Consensus Across Sources:**\n\n- All sources agree on the necessity of providing detailed product information (`id`, `color`, `quantity`, `size`) and shipping address fields (`name`, `address1`, `city`, `state`, `zip`) for obtaining a DTG quote. ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- The requirement of a valid `designId` for an order-ready quote is consistently emphasized. ([scalablepress.com](https://scalablepress.com/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n**Conflicting Information:**\n\n- No significant conflicting information was identified across the sources.\n\n**Information Gaps:**\n\n- � "}],"_meta":{"openai/widgetSessionId":"2b1dd3e4-7d59-4525-b819-c893bae6edc3"},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
